            2026 General Election (10/15/26 Update)



                Home


                Posted on September 14, 2026 | Last Updated on October 15, 2026










    See the latest information for the General Election on Tuesday, November 3, 2026.Tuesday, September 29th – Mail Ballot Drop Box opens and is in front of Barrington Town Hall, 283 County Road (a red, white, and blue flag will be flying to designate the location).Sunday, October 4th – Deadline to register to vote.Tuesday, October 13th – Deadline to apply for a mail ballot.Wednesday, October 14th to Monday, November 2nd (ends at 4:00 PM) – Early voting and emergency mail ballot period.PLEASE NOTE: Early voting is at Barrington Town Hall and the voting hours are the Town Hall’s usual business hours except for the last day (November 2nd) when the polls close at 4:00 PM which is the statewide deadline.Town of Barrington usual business hours:Monday, 8:30 AM to 7:00 PMTuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, 8:30 AM to 4:30 PMFriday, 8:30 AM to noonLOCAL BALLOT QUESTIONS FOR BARRINGTON VOTERSBarrington voters will be asked to consider 4 local ballot questions that propose changes to the Town Charter. These local questions will appear on the ballot as Questions #6 through #9. Information about the 4 local questions is provided in a Local Ballot Questions & Voting in the General Election booklet from the Board of Canvassers and mailed to Barrington residents. See booklet information HERE.STATEWIDE BALLOT QUESTIONS FOR R.I. VOTERSIn addition, the November 3, 2026 ballot includes 5 statewide questions for all R.I. voters to consider. These will appear on the ballot as Questions #1 through #5. Information about these statewide ballot questions is available at the R.I. Secretary of State’s website and select “Publications and Forms” available at https://vote.ri.gov/Election Day voting by precinct is based on your home address, and you can use the Secretary of State’s “Look Up” tool to find your polling location. You can also contact the Clerk’s office at 401-247-1900, ext. 1 to confirm your polling location.The polls in Barrington will open at 7:00 a.m. and close at 8:00 p.m. Any person eligible to vote who is in line at 8:00 p.m. will be allowed to cast their vote before the polls close. Town Clerk’s Office is closed to all business other than Board of Canvassers.----------------Important Information Regarding a CHANGE IN ONE POLLING LOCATION: Precinct #101 - Barrington High School Voters.Due to construction at Barrington High School, the Precinct #101 polling location for the General Election has been CHANGED. For the November 3rd Election, Vote at Barrington Middle School, 261 Middle Highway.ALL OTHER PRECINCTS REMAIN THE SAME.Precinct #101 & #102 - Vote at Barrington Middle School, 261 Middle Highway.Precinct #103 - Vote at Nayatt School, 400 Nayatt Road.Precinct #104 - Vote at Hampden Meadows School, 297 New Meadow Road.Precinct #105 - Vote at Sowams School, 364 Sowams Road.Precinct #106 - Vote at Barrington Town Hall. 283 County Road.Precinct #107 Limited ballot (Statewide races only) and same-day registration - Vote at Barrington Town HallSee the Voting Information Center on the Secretary of State’s website for additional information.









